        "created_at": "2026-05-07 11:40:45",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-11 21:00:18",
        "slug": "jim-perkins",
        "body": "<h2>Pershing Plowshares: custody episodes distinguished</h2><p>The original May 1984 newsletter dates the action and initial detention to April 22, 1984 and reports continued detention while the eight refused bond. The August issue establishes sentencing on July 26, 1984. However, Jim Perkins subsequently described a period of freedom before the trial ended. The initial detention and later sentenced imprisonment are therefore recorded separately; the exact intervening release and later remand dates remain unresolved. The July 26 sentencing date is not silently treated as a new prison-admission date, and no arrest-to-final-release continuous total is inferred.</p><p>The sentence was three years for depredation and five years probation for conspiracy, with restitution. Christin Schmidt expressly corrected the earlier newsletter account of an extra suspended five-year term, and Perkins independently describes the same sentence.</p><p>Sources: <a href=\"https://media.nukeresister.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/NR025_19840509small.pdf#page=2\">Nuclear Resister 25, May 9, 1984, pages 1 and 3</a>; <a href=\"https://media.nukeresister.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/NR026_19840802small.pdf#page=2\">issue 26, August 2, 1984, page 1</a>; <a href=\"https://media.nukeresister.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/NR027_19841203small.pdf#page=11\">issue 27, December 3, 1984, page 10, Schmidt correction</a>; <a href=\"https://objects.lib.uidaho.edu/bpf/turningwheel-spring1986.pdf#page=4\">Buddhist Peace Fellowship, Spring 1986, Perkins firsthand account pages 4-5</a>.</p><p>The Buddhist Peace Fellowship interview conducted in February 1986 explicitly dates his actual release from Danbury to December 23, 1985. This supersedes the December 24 forecast in the December newsletter. His account gives eighteen months served, not a continuous elapsed interval from April 1984. No exact day count is manufactured from the approximate month total. The same publication captions a photograph of Perkins with his daughters; the PDF embeds the entire scanned page rather than a separate original portrait, so the image remains a documented acquisition lead. Source: <a href=\"https://objects.lib.uidaho.edu/bpf/turningwheel-spring1986.pdf#page=6\">BPF Spring 1986, page 6 interview and page 4 photograph</a>.</p><h2>Release day uncertainty preserved</h2><p>The January 20, 1986 Nuclear Resister reports actual parole to the Insight Meditation Society on December 24, 1985, not merely a forecast. The later BPF interview dates release from Danbury to December 23. These may distinguish departure and parole placement, but that distinction is not explicit. This supersedes the preceding exact-day choice: December 1985 is recorded at month precision with December 23-24 bounds. The stored December 1 is a precision placeholder, not an asserted release day. Initial detention and later imprisonment remain separate.</p><p>Sources: <a href=\"https://media.nukeresister.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/NR037_19860120small.pdf#page=7\">Nuclear Resister 37, January 20, 1986, page 6</a>; <a href=\"https://objects.lib.uidaho.edu/bpf/turningwheel-spring1986.pdf#page=6\">BPF Spring 1986 interview, page 6</a>.</p>",
        "under_review": 0,
        "imprisoned_or_exiled": 0,
